                Summary
            </h4>

            <p>
                CRUD represents <strong>Create, Read, Update and Delete</strong>
                operations commonly required for managing application data.
            </p>

            <p>
                Angular can implement CRUD through a service using
                <strong>HttpClient</strong> and the HTTP methods
                <strong>POST, GET, PUT and DELETE</strong>.
            </p>

            <p class="mb-0">
                A typical flow is
                <strong>
                    Angular UI → Component → Service → HttpClient →
                    REST API → Database
                </strong>.
                In the next topic, we will learn how to handle
                <strong>API Responses</strong> properly.
